{"availability":"available","full":"justinjohn0306/MaskGCT-Windows","name":"MaskGCT-Windows","description":"MaskGCT-Windows For Windows Users","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":64,"forks":14,"created":"2024-11-01T14:22:25Z","updated":"2025-05-20T01:48:46Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":[],"demo":"https://maskgct.github.io/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T19:06:49.118Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T19:06:49.118Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T19:06:49.118Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T13:21:15.315Z","stars":64,"forks":14},{"at":"2026-10-12T19:06:49.118Z","stars":64,"forks":14}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["MaskGCT-Windows is a Windows-compatible implementation of MaskGCT: a state-of-the-art, zero-shot, non-autoregressive Text-to-Speech (TTS) model that eliminates the need for explicit text-speech alignment and duration prediction. This implementation allows users to leverage the model's powerful capabilities in a Windows environment.","MaskGCT is a fully non-autoregressive TTS model using a two-stage approach:","MaskGCT generates high-quality, intelligible, and similar speech in a parallel manner. It outperforms other zero-shot TTS models when trained on large-scale, diverse datasets. You can find more details and audio samples on the demo page."],"features":["Predicting semantic tokens from text using a self-supervised learning (SSL) model.","Generating acoustic tokens conditioned on the semantic tokens using a mask-and-predict learning paradigm."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/justinjohn0306/MaskGCT-Windows/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"e36b50137acdf3745c90942fd4f2f42cee1dd2f755a7c7acfd5bde3e6b288133","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T13:21:15.428Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T13:21:15.428Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"MaskGCT-Windows is a Windows-compatible implementation of MaskGCT: a state-of-the-art, zero-shot, n